  - CHANGELOG.md
learnings:
  - A delegated builder typed a field from the rendering it wanted (blocked_on as string[] to .join) rather than from the backend truth (a reason string) — TS accepted it (fetch data is any), build passed, but it's a runtime crash on the first blocked task. When reviewing builder output, grep the field's BACKEND type and the UI's usage; a build-passing type can still be a lie about the data.
  - Stale background serve processes cause phantom smoke-test results (loose:0 when it's really 10). Always pkill -f 'paradigm serve' before a fresh smoke test — a leftover process on a different port served the old dist.
